1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,577
In this town, the king's dragon takes one kid every winter.

2
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:05,329
This year, it picked me.

3
00:00:05,524 --> 00:00:06,722
Everyone told me to run.

4
00:00:06,965 --> 00:00:08,548
I hatched an army instead.

5
00:00:08,845 --> 00:00:11,438
Every kid in town gets an egg on their tenth birthday.

6
00:00:11,642 --> 00:00:13,599
Most hatch a lizard the size of a shoe.

7
00:00:13,871 --> 00:00:17,129
The mayor's son got a hawk, and he hasn't shut up about it since.

8
00:00:17,461 --> 00:00:19,549
My egg sat in the window for a year.

9
00:00:19,731 --> 00:00:20,265
Cold.

10
00:00:20,516 --> 00:00:21,593
Kids called it a rock.

11
00:00:21,833 --> 00:00:23,715
This morning, it cracked down the middle.

12
00:00:23,956 --> 00:00:27,224
Out stepped a bear made of stone, taller than the castle gate.

13
00:00:27,443 --> 00:00:30,393
Then a fox made of smoke, with eyes like lanterns.

14
00:00:30,623 --> 00:00:32,224
The whole square went silent.

15
00:00:32,474 --> 00:00:36,566
Then every lizard in town crawled out of every pocket and lined up behind me.

16
00:00:36,767 --> 00:00:39,857
The mayor's son's hawk flew off his arm and landed on my shoulder.

17
00:00:40,137 --> 00:00:42,796
At noon, forty knights rode in to take my egg.

18
00:00:42,997 --> 00:00:46,251
The captain pointed his lance at me and said, "Hand it over, boy."

19
00:00:46,524 --> 00:00:47,461
The bear stood up.

20
00:00:47,673 --> 00:00:49,499
Its shadow covered the whole square.

21
00:00:49,727 --> 00:00:53,116
The fox circled the knights once, and their war hawks left them too.

22
00:00:53,325 --> 00:00:54,860
Every one of them flew to me.

23
00:00:55,021 --> 00:00:56,884
The knights rode home with empty arms.

24
00:00:57,134 --> 00:00:58,848
Up on his balcony, the king watched.

25
00:00:59,072 --> 00:01:00,112
He didn't say a word.

26
00:01:00,283 --> 00:01:01,276
He just went pale.

27
00:01:01,540 --> 00:01:03,366
But tonight, the egg went dim.

28
00:01:03,604 --> 00:01:05,083
It only has fire for one.

29
00:01:05,345 --> 00:01:06,955
The bear can hold a dragon down.

30
00:01:07,143 --> 00:01:08,716
The fox can steal its fire.

31
00:01:08,943 --> 00:01:10,216
The dragon comes Saturday.

32
00:01:10,383 --> 00:01:11,685
Which one joins my army?

33
00:01:11,866 --> 00:01:13,570
Comment BEAR or FOX.

